==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|scrīptūra||a writing, scripture}}, from {{m|la|scrīptum}}, the supine of {{m|la|scrībō||I write}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The foundational [[text]] of a given religion, or a text considered especially [[holy]].

====Usage notes====
Often used by religious people as a proper noun for their own religion's foundational text.

